{"Title":"An Act authorizing the select board of the town of Provincetown to establish a schedule of fines for parking violations","BillNumber":"S2978","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"JAC0","Name":"Julian Cyr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JAC0","ResponseDate":"2024-11-06T10:07:18.12"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"JAC0","Name":"Julian Cyr","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JAC0","ResponseDate":"2024-11-06T10:07:18.1366667"},{"Id":"SKP1","Name":"Sarah K. Peake","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SKP1","ResponseDate":"2024-04-19T11:47:23.1266667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2978/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"Senate, November 7, 2024 - Substituted as a new draft (Senator Cyr) for the Senate Bill relative to parking violations in the town of Provincetown (Senate, No. 2743).","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Notwithstanding sections 20A or 20A1/2 of chapter 90 of the General Laws or any other general or special law to the contrary, the select board of the town of Provincetown may establish a schedule of fines for parking violations. The fines in said schedule shall not exceed $100; provided, however, that the fine for the violation of parking a motor vehicle: (i) within a posted bus stop shall be $100; (ii) within 10 feet of a fire hydrant shall be not more than $150; and (iii) in violation of handicap parking rules or regulations shall be not more than $300. \r\n\tSECTION 2. The schedule of fines authorized pursuant to section 1 may provide that fines paid: (i) later than 21 days after issuance of the fine but before the parking clerk reports said fine to the registrar pursuant to sections 20A or 20A1/2 of chapter 90 of the General Laws be increased by not more than $25; and (ii) after the parking clerk reports said fine to the registrar pursuant to said sections 20A or 20A1/2 of said chapter 90 be increased by not more than $50. \r\n\tSECTION 3. This act shall take effect upon its passage.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Correctly Drawn","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"S31","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/S31"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Place in OD","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H52","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H52"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Correctly Drawn","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H36","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H36"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}